  "query_preview": "..\n\nSynoptic Setup: Forecast begins with hot high pressure over the \nFour Corners pushing into Wyoming. A broad trough over the western\ntwo-thirds of Canada has broken into two parts with the eastern \ntrough running from northern Manitoba into Ontario and the \nMississippi River Valley. The western part begins over roughly \nsouthern British Columbia and moves south along the shore of the \nPacific Northwest to northern California. In between these two \nairmasses, zonal to SW flow has set up over Montana and the \nIntermountain West. \n\nToday through Monday: Surface high pressure has moved into the \nDakotas this afternoon for light SE to E winds. Zonal flow aloft \nwill gain a more SW tilt with and approaching shortwave \ndisturbance tonight into Monday. The wave will bring isolated \nshowers late tonight into early Monday morning to northeast \nMontana with possibly a few reportable hundredths on the SE side \nof the Yellowstone Valley. Look for somewhat warmer temperatures \non Monday as the system moves to the east. \n\nMonday night into Wednesday: The western most trough will move \ninland and dig into the Intermountain West and Four Corners. In \nresponse the northern section of the flow will build up into a \nridge over Montana that will keep conditions mostly dry through \nthese periods. Tuesday specifically will need to monitored for \nFire Weather concerns due to Low RH and gusty winds as the ridge \nbegins to break down.\n\nWednesday night onwards: A cold front arriving Wednesday into\nWednesday night will allow temps to get cool enough to possibly \ncause frost on river bottoms. People with outside plants that are\nstill alive may wish to bring them in before. Ensemble agreement \nfrom here onward has improved raising confidence slightly \ncompared to yesterday. A ridge in the flow now looks to move in \nFriday and raise temps briefly before a trough follows on swiftly\nthat night. The main models now appear to lose sync around \nSaturday night.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nDeviation to NBM include hourly PoPs for tonight. Main NBM was not\ncapturing output from CAM such as the NAMNest, ARW, and HRRR for \nisolated rain showers across the west and got a partially blended \nupdate from those members. \n\nLow to moderate confidence on chances for showers late tonight \nand early Monday morning. \n\nLow confidence in FireWx Tuesday afternoon. \n\nModerate confidence in partial frost Thursday morning.",
